From 20a70f76f9c5a6393eaacb247fab6927582d5f13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Edukasaun OS <hugomonizdorego@angelinojoana.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:04:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Eduka-Orca: settings window, English default,
 Portuguese/Indonesian/Tetum

New "Eduka-Orca Settings" window (eduka-orca-settings, GTK 3), designed
for users who are hard of hearing or have low vision:
- pages for Home (on/off, quick settings), Language, Speech (speed
  presets, pitch, volume, voice test), Captions (size, colour presets,
  live preview), Reading and typing, Startup, and About
- every change is saved at once and applied live to a running Orca
  through its D-Bus remote controller; language and mouse review offer
  a "Restart now" button
- keyboard navigation everywhere, accessible names and descriptions,
  optional large text and high contrast for the window itself

Languages: English is the default; Portuguese, Indonesian and Tetum are
supported for the settings window (gettext domain eduka-orca) and for
Orca itself (LANGUAGE and EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE set by eduka-orca). Tetum
falls back to Portuguese messages and a European Portuguese voice.

New GSettings schema org.edukasaun.EdukaOrca (language, startup mode
remember/always/never, start delay, welcome message, notifications,
large text, high contrast). eduka-orca-toggle gains --on, --off,
--restart and --status. README.Eduka.md, man page and all script
messages are now in English. Version 50.3+eduka2.

