-## Apa yang berbeda dari Orca biasa
+## What is different from upstream Orca
 
 | | Orca (upstream) | Eduka-Orca |
 |---|---|---|
-| Kecepatan bicara | 50 (dari 0–100) | **30** — lebih pelan, tidak terburu-buru |
-| Nada suara | 5.0 | **4.5** — sedikit lebih rendah, lebih mudah didengar |
-| Volume | 10 (maksimum) | 10 (maksimum) |
-| Teks ucapan di layar (*speech monitor*) | mati | **nyala**, huruf 24 pt, kuning di atas hitam, menempel di bawah layar seperti subtitle, tidak merebut fokus keyboard, kalimat terbaru ditebalkan |
-| Bahasa Tetum | jatuh ke suara Inggris | **memakai suara Portugis (Eropa)** karena eSpeak NG belum punya suara Tetum |
-| Desktop LXQt | tidak ada autostart | autostart LXQt, variabel aksesibilitas Qt, menu *Eduka-Orca*, skrip nyala/mati |
-
-Semua nilai di atas hanya **bawaan**: pengguna tetap bisa mengubahnya di
-*Pengaturan Orca* (Orca+Spasi), dan tombol Orca+Shift+D tetap menyalakan/mematikan
-teks ucapan.
-
-## Cara memakai di Eduka-Desktop
-
-* **Menu → Aksesibilitas → Eduka-Orca**: menyalakan atau mematikan pembaca layar.
-  Muncul notifikasi di layar "Eduka-Orca aktif / nonaktif".
-* Dari terminal: `eduka-orca-toggle`, atau `eduka-orca --replace`.
-* Pengaturan: klik kanan menu *Eduka-Orca → Pengaturan*, atau `eduka-orca --replace --setup`.
-* Pilihan nyala/mati diingat: jika aktif, Eduka-Orca otomatis berjalan saat login
-  (`/etc/xdg/autostart/eduka-orca-autostart.desktop`, khusus LXQt).
-* Pintasan keyboard **Super+Alt+S**: gabungkan
-  `/usr/share/eduka-orca/globalkeyshortcuts-eduka-orca.conf` ke
-  `/etc/xdg/lxqt/globalkeyshortcuts.conf` bawaan Eduka-Desktop.
-
-### Menyalakan secara bawaan untuk semua pengguna (untuk pembuat ISO)
-
-Buat berkas `/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/95_edukasaun-a11y.gschema.override`:
+| Speech rate | 50 (of 0–100) | **30**: slower, words are not rushed |
+| Pitch | 5.0 | **4.5**: slightly lower, easier to hear |
+| Volume | 10 (maximum) | 10 (maximum) |
+| On-screen captions (speech monitor) | off | **on**: 24 pt yellow on black, docked at the bottom of the screen like subtitles, never takes keyboard focus, newest line in bold |
+| Settings | Orca preferences dialog | **Eduka-Orca Settings**, a simple window with one page per topic, plus Orca's own dialog for advanced options |
+| Language | follows the session locale | chosen in Eduka-Orca Settings: **English** (default), Portuguese, Indonesian, Tetum, or the desktop language |
+| Tetum | falls back to an English voice | **European Portuguese voice** (eSpeak NG has no Tetum voice) and Portuguese for Orca messages not yet translated into Tetum |
+| LXQt desktop | no autostart | LXQt autostart with a choice of startup mode, Qt accessibility variables, *Eduka-Orca* menu entry, on/off script |
+
+All the values above are only **defaults**: users can change them in
+Eduka-Orca Settings or in the Orca preferences (Orca+Space), and
+Orca+Shift+D still turns the captions on and off.
+
+## Eduka-Orca Settings
+
+Open it from **Menu → Settings → Eduka-Orca Settings**, from the
+*Settings* action of the *Eduka-Orca* menu entry, or by running
+`eduka-orca-settings` (`--page=speech` opens a specific page).
+
+| Page | What you can change |
+|---|---|
+| Home | Turn the screen reader on or off, speech speed, captions, test the voice; large text and high contrast for the settings window; open the advanced Orca preferences |
+| Language | English, Português, Bahasa Indonesia, Tetun or "Same as the desktop"; switch voices automatically for text in other languages |
+| Speech | Speech on/off, speed (with *Very slow*, *Slow*, *Normal* and *Fast* buttons), pitch, volume, test and reset the voice, punctuation, capital letters, numbers as digits |
+| Captions | Show captions, text size, colour presets (yellow on black, white on black, black on white, black on yellow) or custom colours, with a live preview |
+| Reading and typing | Amount of detail, tutorial messages, reading under the mouse, keyboard layout (desktop/laptop), speaking keys, characters, words and sentences, sounds, braille |
+| Startup | Start at login: *Remember* (default), *Always* or *Never*; wait before starting; welcome message; on/off notifications |
+| About | Version, keyboard shortcuts, reset all settings |
+
+Every change is saved at once; there is no *Apply* button to forget. When the
+screen reader is running, changes are sent to it immediately over D-Bus. Only
+the language and *Read under the mouse* need a restart; the window then offers
+a **Restart now** button.
+
+The window can be used entirely from the keyboard: Tab moves between controls,
+and Ctrl+Page Down / Ctrl+Page Up move between pages. Every control has a
+name and a description for screen readers.
+
+## Using Eduka-Orca on Eduka-Desktop
+
+* **Menu → Accessibility → Eduka-Orca** turns the screen reader on or off.
+  A desktop notification says "Eduka-Orca is on / off".
+* From a terminal: `eduka-orca-toggle` (or `--on`, `--off`, `--restart`,
+  `--status`), or `eduka-orca --replace`.
+* The on/off choice is remembered: with the default *Remember* startup mode,
+  Eduka-Orca starts at login if it was on
+  (`/etc/xdg/autostart/eduka-orca-autostart.desktop`, LXQt only).
+* Keyboard shortcut **Super+Alt+S**: merge
+  `/usr/share/eduka-orca/globalkeyshortcuts-eduka-orca.conf` into the
+  Eduka-Desktop default `/etc/xdg/lxqt/globalkeyshortcuts.conf`.
+
+### Turning it on for every user (for ISO builders)
+
+Create `/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/95_edukasaun-a11y.gschema.override`:
 
 ```
-[org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications]
-screen-reader-enabled=true
+[org.edukasaun.EdukaOrca]
+startup-mode='always'
 ```
 
-lalu jalankan `glib-compile-schemas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas`.
+then run `glib-compile-schemas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas`.
 
-### Mengubah kecepatan bawaan untuk seluruh sistem
+### Changing the defaults system-wide
 
-Buat berkas override, misalnya `96_edukasaun-orca.gschema.override`:
+Create an override file, for example `96_edukasaun-orca.gschema.override`:
 
 ```
+[org.edukasaun.EdukaOrca]
+language='tet'
+
 [org.gnome.Orca.Voice]
 rate=25
 pitch=4.5
@@ -60,39 +89,49 @@ pitch=4.5
 monitor-font-size=28
 ```
 
