-
-## English summary
-
-Eduka-Orca = Orca 50.3 + these changes: speech rate 30 (upstream 50), pitch 4.5
-(upstream 5.0), speech monitor captions on by default (24 pt yellow on black,
-docked at the bottom, never steals focus, newest line bold, persisted in
-GSettings key `org.gnome.Orca.Speech monitor-enabled`), Tetum locale uses a
-European Portuguese voice, plus LXQt autostart, Qt accessibility environment,
-an "Eduka-Orca" menu entry and an on/off toggle script. Built for Debian 13
-(trixie), which Edukasaun OS follows.
+`language` is one of `en` (default), `pt`, `id`, `tet` or `system`.
+
+## Languages
+
+* The settings window is translated with gettext (domain `eduka-orca`,
+  files in `eduka/po/`). English is the source language.
+* Orca's own messages come from upstream Orca translations (`po/pt.po`,
+  `po/id.po`). There is no full Tetum translation of Orca yet: `po/tet.po`
+  holds the Eduka strings, and everything else falls back to Portuguese.
+* The voice follows the chosen language. The `eduka-orca` launcher exports
+  `EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE`, which Orca uses even if the matching system locale is
+  not installed. Tetum is spoken with a European Portuguese voice.
+* The Tetum translations were written for Edukasaun OS and should be reviewed
+  by Tetum speakers; corrections to `eduka/po/tet.po` are welcome.
+
+## Files installed by this package
+
+* `/usr/bin/orca`: Orca 50.3 with the Eduka patches
+* `/usr/bin/eduka-orca`, `eduka-orca-settings`, `eduka-orca-toggle`,
+  `eduka-orca-autostart`
+* `/usr/share/eduka-orca/eduka_orca_settings/`: the settings window
+* `/usr/share/applications/eduka-orca.desktop`,
+  `eduka-orca-settings.desktop`: menu entries
+* `/etc/xdg/autostart/eduka-orca-autostart.desktop`: LXQt autostart
+* `/etc/profile.d/eduka-orca-a11y.sh`, `/usr/lib/environment.d/90-eduka-orca-a11y.conf`:
+  `QT_ACCESSIBILITY=1` so that Qt/LXQt applications can be read by Orca
+* `/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/org.edukasaun.EdukaOrca.gschema.xml`,
+  `90_eduka-orca.gschema.override`
+* `/usr/share/locale/{id,pt,tet}/LC_MESSAGES/eduka-orca.mo`
+
+## A note about hearing loss
+
+Orca is a **speech**-based screen reader. For people who are **deaf**, speech
+does not help; what helps are the **on-screen captions**, which are on by
+default, together with screen magnification and a high-contrast theme. For
+people who are **hard of hearing**, slow speech, a lower pitch and full volume
+make speech easier to follow. Testing with hard-of-hearing students at school
+is strongly recommended to find the speech rate that suits them best.
+
+## Source code
+
+Based on tag `50.3` of https://github.com/GNOME/orca (LGPL-2.1-or-later).
+Every Eduka change is marked with an `Eduka-Orca` comment. Defaults are in
+`src/orca/eduka_defaults.py`, the settings window is in `eduka/settings/`,
+and the checks are in `tests/unit_tests/test_eduka_defaults.py` and
+`tests/unit_tests/test_eduka_settings.py`.
diff --git a/eduka/bin/eduka-orca b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca
index ef68b62..0297c90 100755
--- a/eduka/bin/eduka-orca
+++ b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca
@@ -1,8 +1,15 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 # Eduka-Orca launcher for Eduka-Desktop (LXQt) on Edukasaun OS.
 #
-# Starts Orca with the Eduka defaults (slow speech, on-screen captions). All
-# arguments are passed through to orca, e.g. "eduka-orca --replace --setup".
+# Starts Orca with the Eduka defaults (slow speech, on-screen captions) in the
+# language chosen in Eduka-Orca Settings (English by default). All arguments
+# are passed through to orca, e.g. "eduka-orca --replace --setup".
+
+EDUKA_SCHEMA=org.edukasaun.EdukaOrca
+
+eduka_get() {
+    gsettings get "$EDUKA_SCHEMA" "$1" 2>/dev/null | tr -d "'"
+}
 
 # Qt applications (the whole LXQt desktop) expose their accessibility tree to
 # AT-SPI only when this is set. It is also exported session-wide by
@@ -14,4 +21,48 @@ if command -v gsettings >/dev/null 2>&1; then
     gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface toolkit-accessibility true 2>/dev/null || true
 fi
 
+# Language of Orca's messages and voice. "system" keeps the session's locale.
+# Orca has no Tetum translation yet, so Tetum falls back to Portuguese messages;
+# its voice is European Portuguese (see src/orca/eduka_defaults.py).
+language=$(eduka_get language)
+case "${language:-en}" in
+    en) export LANGUAGE=en EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE=en ;;
+    pt) export LANGUAGE=pt:pt_BR EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE=pt ;;
+    id) export LANGUAGE=id EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE=id ;;
+    tet) export LANGUAGE=tet:pt:pt_BR EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE=tet ;;
+    *) language=system ;;
+esac
+
+welcome_text() {
+    case "${EDUKA_ORCA_LANGUAGE:-${LANGUAGE:-${LC_ALL:-${LC_MESSAGES:-$LANG}}}}" in
+        tet*) echo "Eduka-Orca prontu ona" ;;
+        pt*) echo "O Eduka-Orca está pronto" ;;
+        id*) echo "Eduka-Orca siap" ;;
+        *) echo "Eduka-Orca is ready" ;;
+    esac
+}
+
+# Say (and caption) a short welcome once Orca's D-Bus service is up.
+welcome=$(eduka_get welcome-message)
+case " $* " in
+    *" --setup "* | *" -s "* | *" --help "* | *" -h "* | *" --version "* | *" -v "*)
+        welcome=false ;;
+esac
+if [ "${welcome:-true}" = "true" ] && command -v gdbus >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    message=$(welcome_text)
+    (
+        tries=0
+        while [ "$tries" -lt 30 ]; do
+            sleep 1
+            tries=$((tries + 1))
+            if gdbus call --session --dest org.gnome.Orca.Service \
+                --object-path /org/gnome/Orca/Service \
+                --method org.gnome.Orca.Service.PresentMessage "$message" \
+                >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+                break
+            fi
